cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "src_method: Successive Randomized Compression for tensor networks"
message: "If you use this software, please cite both this software and the paper that introduced the SRC algorithm."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Panadés-Barrueta"
    given-names: "Ramón L."
    affiliation: "Algorithmiq Ltd."
  - family-names: "Botelho"
    given-names: "Ludmila"
    affiliation: "Algorithmiq Ltd."
repository-code: "https://github.com/Algorithmiq/src-method"
url: "https://docs.algorithmiq.fi/src-method"
abstract: >-
  An implementation of the Successive Randomized Compression (SRC) algorithm
  for matrix product states and matrix product operators, covering MPO-MPS and
  MPO-MPO contraction-compression as well as standalone MPS and MPO
  compression, with CPU (NumPy) and GPU (CuPy) backends.
keywords:
  - tensor networks
  - matrix product states
  - matrix product operators
  - randomized linear algebra
  - quantum simulation
license: Apache-2.0
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: "Successive randomized compression: A randomized algorithm for the compressed MPO-MPS product"
  authors:
